    (ROOT / 'RESULTS.md').write_text(f"# The drilling process may leave a measurable tissue state\n\nThe executable results carry thermal dose, regional damage and later biological measurements by a HANDOVER-kant.\nTwo local primary studies are reference observations. They establish useful process–tissue relationships, but does not provide any validated\nprediction of human healing weeks or implantation ISQ, a measure from resonance rate analysis.\n\n| Question | Faktiskt svar | Resolution and Reference Observations |\n|---|---|---|\n| What does the sensor's binary temperature flag miss? | Sex numeriskt beskrivna regioner har cirka 0,2–1,1 mm skada trots associerade sondtoppar under 47 °C. | Skada PER_SURFACE_REGION; sond PER_POINT. [Pourgiv et al.](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e26248), Table 2 and the paragraphs p0105/p0110. |\n| Which observed protocol reaches the study's smallest reported damage width? | Ultraljudsborrning, 2000 rpm, 60 mm/min, 4 mm borr, 20 kHz, 20 µm amplitud: cirka 0,2 mm in both cortical and spongious leg. | PER_SURFACE_REGION, samma studie p0110. Medelkraft 4,05 ± 0,30 N. Cooling and uncertainty of the width are missing. |\n| Is there a biological outcome after the drilling? | Hundbenfragment: 500 mot 1000 rpm har {v['viability_500minus1000_percentage_points']:.2f} percentage point higher viability today 3-Assay and {v['yield_day14_500_over1000']:.6f}× Larger cell growth at two weeks of culture. | POPULATION, n=4 rapporterade gruppprov. [Zhou et al.](https://doi.org/10.1186/s12903-023-03611-w), Sec21 And Fig. 5e/f. |\n| Can the temperature leave a spatial state? | 28 befintliga K3-fields export residual tissue dose with coordinates and worms. Dry L10-modell ger 0,15 mm lateral screeningzon. | PER_POINT, 0,1 mm gitter. Egen befintlig simulering; empirisk temperaturmagnitud har fallit i K3. |\n| What humane speeds, cooling, sequences, and forces keep the damage below a published safe limit for a given bone? | UNKNOWN. | No applicable validated limit or parade process–skada–The healing model is found in the substrate. |\n| How many weeks of healing delay or which ISQ- Progress is predicted? | UNKNOWN. | The supporting biological transfer act and a matched external reference observation are missing. |\n\n**0,2 mm is an observed comparator, no biological safety limit.** The oval study concerns ex vivo bone\nvid 22 °C. Its damage is defined as an area with more than 90 % tomma osteocytlakuner. Tre protokoll har numeriska\nwidths without: SDLower temperature at a distant probe therefore gives no guarantee of the state of the entire tissue.\nProbe and cortical histology are not securely co-located; mechanical damage, starting viability and sample preparation may be\ndoes not separate. The result drops the sensor as the sole total damage description, but does not shed a local thermal law\nat the actual drilling wall.\n\nThe dog trial involves harvested mandibulary fragments with: 1 mm drill without flushing. T10 is one 10- second-second measuring windows,\nno complete temperature history. 3 is an assay time; the exact displacement from the operation is\nnot established here. Cell outgrowth concerns two weeks of culture. ALP is measured after one week of osteogenic induction and\nmineralisering efter 21 day induction: these times must not be marked as post-operative healing days.\nThe biological measurements refer to bone fragments, not remaining bones around an implant.\n\nSD and n=4 provides, under the assumption of independent normalised replicated margin t range.\ntheir endpoints become {lo:.3f}–{hi:.3f} percentage points for 500 mot 1000 rpm. This is not a pair 95 %-intervall.\nThe group funds for viability and ALP have different rank, but the viability intervals overlap in all three rank turns.\nThe frozen the validation gate for mid-range compliance falls; a causal skill difference does not follow from this check.\n\nPublished risk support exists, but it does not close the numerical link. [Eriksson 1984](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6593442/)\nprovides a qualitative bone growth anchor at constant 44/47/50 °C under en minut. [Kniha 2022](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-25581-9),\nTable 2/Results, describes necrosis and bone contact after seven days in rats. [Kniha 2023](https://doi.org/10.1186/s13005-023-00349-2),\nFig. 4B, reports no statistically secured hot ISQ-fall after seven days; it does not mean shown absence\nMiniature implants, various tissue support and missing paired time series prevent transfer to humane weeks.\n\n| Grind eller bortfall | Redovisat utfall |\n|---|---|\n| R1, fulla temperaturhistorier | 12/12 saknas: exakt dosvalidering UNKNOWN. |\n| R1, numeriska skadeprotokoll | 3/12 kept; 9/12 None of the six method pairs have both widths. |\n| R2, ovina observationer till K3 | 6/6 rejected: other population and process. No data lending calibration. |\n| R2, robust breddvillkor | 6/6 two regions reach nominally 0,2 The mm comparison. |\n| R3, grupprelationer | 4/4 kept. 4/4 individual/point relationships; and 4/4 wall/ISQTransfers are rejected. |\n| R3, fryst viabilitetskontrast | 39,10 pp faller med 1,51 The pp: number applies 50 mot 1000 rpm but noticed 500 mot 1000. Originalet bevaras. |\n| R4, new physiological measurements | 0Own fixture only tests software. |\n\nEqually informed table spreads and integration controls reproduce the result. No algorithm advantage is claimed.\nMisinjections precipitate temperature controls, dose/width/cell count units, missing kalibrering/region,\nremoved tissue, wrong sample identity and fake security or ISQValid technical checks are holding.\nSource-outcome disclosure is available in the freezer files: R3:s results were already read when the hypothesis was frozen.\nopen reconstruction and a new information interface, no blind prediction validation.\n\nRun `./run_all.sh`. It recreates crude excerpts, tables, remaining dose fields, figures and manifests without network.\n`bench_handover.py` can read a real calibrated CSV. The integral is exactly for the linear temperature interpolant;\nThe sensor limits do not bind unsampled peaks and the dose is still a phenomenological liability for tissue measurement.\nMINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_CONTRACT.json describes the next same-test design: temperature history, final histology\nEarly destructive measurements need separate cohorts and must not be given the same individual identity.\n\nThe graph's existing goals are found in interfaces.jsonl. Rank, pack and floptch provided STALE_INPUT; inga grafer byggdes om.\nGRAPH_FEEDBACK.json is PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW and needs to be tied when the graph owner made the view up to date.\n")
    (ROOT / 'README_DEMO.md').write_text("# From drilling to measurable tissue state\n\nThe idea is to leave an explicit state after drilling: local thermal dose, regional observed damage and\nseparate biological measurements. The demonstration shows what published data can determine and where the healing model\nstill missing support.\n\n```bash\n./run_all.sh\n```\n\nRequires Python 3, numpy, scipy, matplotlib and the existing local sources in SOURCE_MANIFEST.json. No installation\nor network download is done. Maximum four threads. The result is available in RESULTS.md and machine readable in results.json.\n\n| Results | External reference |\n|---|---|\n| Three oval protocols have reported regional damage of about 0,2 – 1,1 mm . | Heliyon 2024, p0105/p0110; PER_SURFACE_REGION. |\n| UD 2000 rpm/60 mm/min has approximately 0,2 mm in both tissue types. | Same study, p0110. Observed comparison value, no safe boundary. |\n| 500 against 1000 rpm has 37,59 pp higher viability and 3,483 × cell growth at two weeks of culture. | Dog bone fragments, n=4 group samples; BMC 2023, Fig. 5e/f; POPULATION. |\n| 28 existing dose fields are given an interface for the remaining tissue. | K3 simulation; empirical temperature magnitude failed. |\n| Human safe drill parameters, healing weeks and ISQ. | UNKNOWN. |\n\n![Published measurements and biological handover](figures/X28_measured_handover.png)\n\nWhat does not holds : sensor temperature does not describe total regional damage; bone fragments is not implant wall;\nthree approximate damage widths cannot be a safe human boundary. Growing/induction days are not healing days.\nR3 : s frozen 39,10 pp contrast was mislabeled and fails ; the correct observation is 37,59 pp. Original retained.\nR3 : s source output had been read before the freeze, which is reported. No independent lab replication was performed.\nCustom fixture is only used for import, unit and identity checks.\n\nFor a real temperature measurement, fill BENCH_THERMAL_TEMPLATE.csv :\n\n```bash\npython3 bench_handover.py --thermal MIN_MATNING.csv --out MIN_HANDOVER.json\n```\n\nCSV requires the entire measuring window, calibration limit, pro placement, specimen /region/ tissue and remaining masks. All\npoint identities retained. The final histology of the same test can be linked to `join_injury`. No unknown healing stroke\nfilled in. Measurement requirements and identification limitations are available in MINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_CONTRACT.json .\n\nLicenses: [Pourgiv et al., Heliyon 2024](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e26248) states CC BY-NC-ND 4.0\nfor the article. Only numerical facts are read and quoted; original characters and full text are not republished.\n[Zhou et al., BMC 2023 ](https://doi.org/10.1186/s12903-023-03611-w) indicates CC BY 4.0 ; extract and custom figures\nare processings of reported measurements . K3 is the project's own simulation. Its former ToothFairy2 background\nspecified CC BY - SA in the project data; no ToothFairy2 cases are read or exported in this round. No patient data are used.\n")
    (ROOT / 'HANDOFF.md').write_text("# X28 — four completed designs\n\nCapability : a command builds external damage measurements, the later biological measurement channels of bone fragments and 28 existing\ndose field as remaining tissue state. Calibrated laboratory histories can be imported with specific/region/time contracts.\nThe final goal — given bone type/process to damage limit, human healing weeks and ISQ — is still UNKNOWN.\n\nR1 : 12 temperature protocol is retained. 12 / 12 full dose stories are missing. Six numeric damage areas are missed by low\nprobe temperature. Sensor-only total injury fails ; the local thermal law at the drilling wall does not fold.\n3 / 12 protocols have numerical width; 0 / 6 method pairs have both numerical widths.\nR2 : 28 fields are exported with remaining masks. Dry L10 model: 0,15 mm lateral screening width of 0,1 mm grid .\nK3 : s empirical temperature gate is still FAIL . 6 / 6 ovina-to-K3-joins are rejected. UD 2000/60 has approximately 0.2 mm in\nboth tissue types. There is no robust width uncertainty or human safety limit.\nR3 : four group links from dog bone fragments. 37,59 pp viability contrast 500 -minus -1000 and 3,483221 × cell growth\nat two weeks of culture. Frozen 39,10 pp FAIL with 1,51 pp: error group label. All freeze files remain. Mean rank gate FAIL;\nall three reverse viability pairs have overlapping ranges. 4 / 4 point/individual and 4 / 4 wall -/ ISQ transfers are rejected.\nAssay/induction days are different from post-operative time; SOURCE_TIMING_CORRECTION.json retains the clarification.\nR4 : exact integral of linear T(t), dose range and same specific/region/tissue/population-join run. 47 ° C/60 s\nprovides 16 CEM43 - min ; 44 ° C / 60 s provides 2 . Own fixture verifies only software. Zero new physical specimen.\nTechnical controls and error injections holds. No independent physiological prediction validation has been performed.\n\nNext construction: same osteotomy site through calibrated heat history, final histology and serial stability,\nwith pre-registered damage/contact team and independent specimen for validation. Two thermopoints see a gradient but\ndoes not generally identify all heat source/cooling parameters. Early destructive assays require a separate cohort;\nNever connect them as the same individual specimen . Use MINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_CONTRACT.json and bench_handover.py.\nRun no further scalar temperature ranking as replacement for these missing measurements .\n\nGraph: DENT-IF-TH-BONE-TEMP-FIELD found in notes/expansion/interfaces.jsonl. Working rank/packet/dispatch returned\nSTALE_INPUT. No rebuild or source/ generated graph mutation was performed. GRAPH_FEEDBACK.json is\nPENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. Missing coverage: native receiving node for residual tissue damage condition\nwith PER_POINT/PER_SURFACE_REGION support and a separate HANDOVER healing resolution. The ISQ consumer aggregates to\nimplant / PER_TOOTH only after contact geometry and calibrated time course. When the graph owner made the view fresh:\nDispatch X28 -heat-osseo with TASK_BRIEF.md and connect feedback to the current results.json -hash.\n")
